templates.body:
Draft a tax memo for {{client_name}} ({{jurisdiction}}, tax year {{tax_year}}). Structure: Issue, Facts, Analysis, Recommendation, Open questions. Use only the rules and rates I paste below; where a rule is needed that I did not give, write [rule needed] instead of guessing. Show every calculation step.

Rules and rates:
{{rules}}

Facts:
{{facts}}

Write the scope section of an engagement letter for {{client_name}}: services included ({{services}}), services excluded, the client's responsibilities (records, deadlines, accuracy), our responsibilities, fees ({{fees}}) and timeline. Plain, unambiguous language; no promises about outcomes.

Context:
{{context}}

Analyse the budget-versus-actual figures below for {{client_name}}, period {{period}}. For each line with a variance above {{threshold}}: amount, percentage, likely driver from my notes, and whether it looks one-off or recurring. Finish with a five-sentence management summary. Recompute every percentage; do not trust mine.

Figures:
{{figures}}

Notes:
{{notes}}

Write an email to {{client_name}} requesting the documents still missing for {{purpose}}, due {{deadline}}. Friendly and firm, a checklist with one line per item and why it is needed, and what happens if the deadline passes.

Missing items:
{{items}}
